<section id="stop">
 <h2>What happens at every stop</h2>
 <p>The turntable turns 45° and waits until it is completely still. Then the four cameras take their photos one after another. Each light flashes only while its own camera takes the photo.</p>
 <p>Why one at a time: all four lights point at the same part. A light that is on during another camera's photo shows up in that photo as a bright reflection, and a reflection can hide a defect or look like one.</p>
